\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen surges to four-year high against dollar.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Christina Fincher  \par \uc2 586 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 12:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates price action, adds Tanigaki comments, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  data)  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, March 31 (Reuters) - The yen surged to a four-year high against the dollar on Wednesday as investors bet a recovering economy would prompt \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to step back from heavy yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the new fiscal year.  \par \par \uc2 The yen rose at breakneck speed after hurdling 105 per dollar, previously considered the tolerance threshold for Japan which has been keen to prevent a strengthening yen jeopardising its export-led recovery.  \par \par \uc2 Comments from Japanese Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki that Japan had grown resilient to the stronger yen gave the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  another boost in the European session, lifting it to 103.45 to the dollar - its highest since April 2000.  \par \par \uc2 "The dollar's break through 105 yen implies more acceptance of yen strength from Japanese policymakers," said Bilal Hafeez, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Deutsche Bank.  \par \par \uc2 "Economic fundamentals are pointing to further yen strength and it will be harder for \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to justify \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."  \par \par \uc2 By 1030 GMT, the yen was off session peaks at 103.90, but still on track for its sharpest one-day rise against the dollar this year.  \par \par \uc2 Official data showed Japan threw more than 4.7 trillion yen at the foreign exchanges in March, bringing its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the start of this year to more than 15 trillion yen. That followed a record of 20 trillion yen in calendar 2003.  \par \par \uc2 The euro outperformed the dollar but also succumbed to broad-based yen strength, falling more than one percent to 126.63, its lowest since last November.  \par \par \uc2 JAPAN OPTIMISM  \par \par \uc2 Expectation of continuing improvement in Japan's economic outlook also supported the yen as investors positioned for a robust quarterly "tankan" business survey from the Bank of Japan at 2350 GMT.  \par \par \uc2 A Reuters poll forecast the survey would reveal heightened optimism among big manufacturers who are benefiting from robust exports and high-tech demand.  \par \par \uc2 Although the Bank of Japan was suspected of selling yen for dollars in Tokyo hours, the size appeared relatively small compared to recent massive \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Nevertheless, not everyone was convinced \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would suddenly walk away from its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy.  \par \par \uc2 "It's hard to believe they're going to let dollar/yen go into freefall. The line in the sand at 105 has gone, clearly, but I wouldn't be surprised to see another one above 100," said Lee Ferridge, head of global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at Rabobank in London.  \par \par \uc2 EURO OUTPERFORMS DOLLAR  \par \par \uc2 The euro was up nearly half a percent against the dollar at $1.2216, slightly below earlier one-week highs but up two cents from 2004 lows hit on Monday.  \par \par \uc2 News of a fire at a BP Plc refinery in Texas bolstered the euro against the dollar in early trade. The FBI had last week warned of a security threat to refiners in that area, but a BP spokeswoman said there was no sign of outside influence.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said dimming expectations of an interest rate cut from the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday were also supporting the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "Expectations for an ECB rate cut are now much reduced, and euro/dollar has benefited from that," said Adam Cole, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Credit Agricole Indosuez.  \par \par \uc2 The Chicago purchasing managers' index, due at 1500 GMT, is forecast to show a fall to 61.5 in March from 63.6 in February.  \par \par \uc2 However, reaction to the data may be muted ahead of Friday's key U.S. payroll report, dealers said.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040331e03v001cs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
