\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  March  \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention \highlight\uc2  Y4.7026 trln-MOF.  \b0\par\par\uc2 170 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 12:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, March 31 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold 4.7026 trillion yen in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in March - equivalent to $45.24 billion at Wednesday's rate - in an attempt to stem the yen's rise against the dollar, \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed.  \par \par \uc2 The total, which covers the period from February 26 to March 29, compares with 3.342 trillion yen sold in February to ease pressure on Japanese exporters from a strong yen.  \par \par \uc2 The March data means the Japanese authorities sold 15.1991 trillion yen in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the January-March period.  \par \par \uc2 That followed an annual record of 20 trillion yen in calendar 2003.  \par \par \uc2 Within the period covered by the figure, the dollar fell to 105.20 yen on March 29, a 6.7 percent decline from the peak during the month of 112.32 yen marked on March 8. It fell as low as 103.40 yen on Wednesday, but at the time the figure was announced was around 103.95 yen.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040331e03v0019m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
