\par\par \b \uc2 Yen soars above 105/dlr despite Japan jawboning.   \b0\par\par\uc2 485 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 07:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, March 31 (Reuters) - Japan's apparent line of defence against the strength of the yen succumbed on Wednesday to growing optimism about the Japanese economy and talk that the government no longer needed to aggressively beat down the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 On the final day of the fiscal year and a day ahead of the release of a closely watched business survey, the yen broke above 105 to the dollar for the first time since September 2000 on talk that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  need not, and would not, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  as heavily as it has since last year as its economic recovery gathers pace.   \par \par \uc2 "With recent economic indicators coming in strong and Japanese share prices rising, the authorities may be thinking they don't need to be particular about the 105 yen level," said Tohru Sasaki, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at JP Morgan Chase in Tokyo.   \par \par \uc2 The 105 level has been long seen as the most important line of defence for officials worried that a strong yen could derail the economy's economic recovery after a decade of malaise.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  has spent 30 trillion yen ($284 billion) in yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the start of 2003.   \par \par \uc2 Many Japanese exporters such as Canon Inc (7751.T), Japan's largest maker of office machines, and electronics giant Sony Corp (6758.T) have made 105 yen the basis of their profit-target planning for the 2004/05 business year starting on Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 Still, talk has surfaced recently that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  could scale back its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaign from the start of the new fiscal year.   \par \par \uc2 Japanese officials have denied any such plan. "As we have been saying repeatedly, the idea that we will change our \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy after a certain point in time is merely speculation," a senior MOF official told Reuters on Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 The government's top spokesman, Chief Cabinet Secretary Yasuo Fukuda, also said the government would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  as it saw fit.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  figures for March will be released at 1000 GMT.   \par \par \uc2 The market, paying little heed to the MOF warning, pushed the yen above 104 to the dollar by 0420 GMT, its highest level since June 2000, helped by expectations of more positive news on the economy on Thursday when the Bank of Japan releases its quarterly "tankan" corporate sentiment survey.   \par \par \uc2 Japanese share prices remained firm despite the yen's rise.   \par \par \uc2 The Nikkei average was down 0.13 percent at 11,678.40 at midday, not far from its recent 22-month high.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  so far has been greeted with scorn by some policy makers abroad, notably by Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan.   \par \par \uc2 Greenspan said earlier this month that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would have to slow and eventually cease.   \par \par \uc2 Many U.S. businesses also say that keeping the yen artificially weak gives Japan an unfair trade advantage, and destroys the jobs of American workers.   \par \par \uc2 ($1=105.81 yen).    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040331e03v000f9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
