\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Options: Yen Volatilities Ease As Dollar Recovers  \b0\par\par\uc2 434 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 20:35\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--Volatilities implied by one-month dollar/yen \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  options eased back from overnight highs Wednesday in New York trade as the dollar recovered from four-year lows against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot market.  \par \par \uc2 Dollar/yen option volatilities soared to their highest level since September 2001 during Tokyo trade as the dollar slid over two yen to Y103.44 amid an apparent withdrawal of Japanese monetary authorities from the market.  \par \par \uc2 Speculation had been rampant that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , would back away from its strategy of large-scale \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  once the fiscal year ended Wednesday, but the severity of the move still caught investors by surprise.  \par \par \uc2 Still, the dollar has since recovered back above Y104 in a generally quiet North American session.  \par \par \uc2 Wednesday afternoon, the dollar was trading at Y104.22, still down sharply from Y105.64 late Tuesday. The euro was at $1.2300, up from $1.2165, while it was lower against the yen at Y128.24 versus Y128.56.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, implied volatility was "far outstripping the pace of the move as measured from intraday spot data," said London dealers in a research piece, noting that actual volatility had only ticked slightly higher. Thus, their options models were sending a "very strong" sell signal for volatilities.  \par \par \uc2 One-month at-the-money dollar/yen options implied volatility of 12.20%/12.60%, below 12.90%/13.10% earlier in Tokyo, but still well above 11.70%/12.00% in New York Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 Volatilities on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  options gauge the anticipated moves in the underlying \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with a higher volatility implying a wider trading range.  \par \par \uc2 One-month at-the-money euro/dollar options implied volatility of 11.70%/12.00%, unchanged from levels seen earlier in Tokyo, but above 11.50%/11.80% in New York Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 One-month euro/yen option volatilities were at 13.55%/13.85%, versus 13.35%/13.75% in Tokyo and 14.35%/15.35% in New York Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 One-month risk-reversals on dollar/yen favor yen calls at 2.3%/2.7% steady from levels in Tokyo but above 2.1%/2.4% in New York. Risk-reversals measure the market preference for either put or call options by the premium or discount applied.  \par \par \uc2 Euro calls were favored by -0.1%/0.3%, versus being neutral at -0.2%/0.2% the day before.  \par \par \uc2 -By Tom Barkley, Dow Jones Newswires; 201-938-4385; tom.barkley@dowjones.com [ 31-03-04 1835GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1077 4127 44427  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040331e03v000zv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
