\par\par \b \uc2 Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dollar Drops Sharply To 4-Year Low Vs Yen  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Jonathan Soble  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 872 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 07:42\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Japan's fiscal year came to a dizzying end in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets Wednesday, as the dollar plunged nearly two yen to a four-year low against its Japanese counterpart.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar took just a few seconds to tumble much of the distance to Y103.97, its lowest level since June 2000. The move caught Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities and many traders off-guard, and was attributed to speculators, who triggered stop-loss sell orders at and below Y105 - a "line in the sand" that had held for more than three years.  \par \par \uc2 "Non-Japanese speculators were saying since this morning they were going to try taking on the MOF," a European bank dealer said, referring to Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "It seems they succeeded."  \par \par \uc2 The sellers, said chiefly to be U.S.-based hedge funds, essentially challenged the ministry to defend the dollar amid growing market speculation that Tokyo has abandoned its policy of aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 But the MOF declined to take up the fight.  \par \par \uc2 Some traders said the authorities sold a small amount of yen to check the dollar's fall, but there was little sign of serious \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "They're definitely not trying to push it back up," a senior Tokyo brokerage dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 He said dollar sellers may have taken their cue to pounce from news of an explosion at a Texas oil refinery. A furnace fire apparently sparked the explosion at the British Petroleum facility on the Gulf Coast, forcing the evacuation of the plant. There were no reports of injuries.  \par \par \uc2 Speculators acted on initial reports, before the cause or seriousness of the explosion could be determined, he said.  \par \par \uc2 Japanese Prime Minister Junichiro Koizumi brushed off questions about the dollar's fall, telling reporters: "Ask the market."  \par \par \uc2 But other officials, including Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki, insisted the government would take steps against excessive movements if necessary.  \par \par \uc2 "We believe \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates should move stably in reflection of fundamentals, and if movements stop reflecting fundamentals, we will take appropriate action," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Tokyo has been all but absent from the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets since it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily to drive the dollar as high as Y112.30 earlier this month. A string of local and international media reports have suggested that officials are more confident that Japan's economic recovery can withstand an appreciation of the yen.  \par \par \uc2 Wednesday's plunge in the dollar through multiple chart support levels brought even further falls in sight.  \par \par \uc2 Technical analysis suggested the U.S. unit has no strong chart support before the area around Y101.27-43, where it bottomed between December 1999 and January 2000.  \par \par \uc2 "If there's no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it's not impossible for the dollar to try Y102 and then Y101" in the next few days, said Tatsuro Karitani, a vice president for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Mizuho Corporate Bank.  \par \par \uc2 At 0515 GMT, the dollar was quoted at Y104.35, compared with Y105.64 late Tuesday in New York. The dollar was at Y105.59 late Tuesday in Tokyo.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was at $1.2219, up from $1.2165 late Tuesday in New York. The euro was at $1.2177 in Tokyo Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y127.53, down from Y128.56 in New York Tuesday. The euro was at Y128.58 in Tokyo Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 Sterling was at $1.8319, up from $1.8265 in New York and higher than $1.8208 Tuesday in Tokyo. [ 31-03-04 0542GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Speculators may also have been betting that the MOF would stick to a past pattern of shunning \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the last day of the fiscal year.  \par \par \uc2 Tohru Sasaki, a strategist at J.P. Morgan in Tokyo, said the ministry hadn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on March 31 for eight years through 2003. That's despite the fact the MOF has often fought hard to keep the yen from strengthening as the end the of the fiscal year has approached.  \par \par \uc2 Tokyo officials may fear being accused of blatant market manipulation if they push the yen down on the day Japanese firms - many with large overseas asset holdings - close their books.  \par \par \uc2 A similar concern is motivating the MOF to withdraw from \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets now, Sasaki said.  \par \par \uc2 "They probably believe it's better to let Y105 break than to risk angering the U.S." with heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he said. "The economy's upswing makes that easier."  \par \par \uc2 MOF officials, however, stuck to their standard script on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 In addition to threatening to act if exchange rates diverged from fundamentals, Tanigaki told Parliament that talk that the U.S. has pressured \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  was unfounded.  \par \par \uc2 -By Jonathan Soble, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; jonathan.soble@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Kirsty Mackenzie and John Gibson  \par \par \uc2 The chart of late Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates that accompanied Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been replaced with an enhanced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixture that is updated hourly.  \par \par \uc2 Subscribers can find this table:  \par \par \uc2 -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087.  \par \par \uc2 -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX  \par \par \uc2 -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT  \par \par \uc2 -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX [ 31-03-04 0621GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1074  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040331e03v0006y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
