\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro bounces back ahead of ECB, yen firm.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Natsuko Waki  \par \uc2 538 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 09:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, March 30 (Reuters) - The euro bounced higher on Tuesday in jittery trading ahead of a euro zone interest rate decision this week, while the yen held firm, supported by expectations for a solid economic recovery in Japan. Investors were reluctant to tilt their positions either way ahead of big events later in the week including a European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meeting and Japan's "tankan" survey of business sentiment, both on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 Friday brings keenly-awaited U.S. non-farm payroll figures, which are expected to show that U.S. companies are finally hiring aggressively - which could raise expectations for a quicker end to the Federal Reserve's low-rates stance.  \par \par \uc2 Recent comments by ECB officials increased expectations the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might be preparing the ground for a rate cut as soon as this week, taking the euro down to this year's low on Monday, but some say selling might have been overdone.  \par \par \uc2 "We are basically waiting for three important things to happen this week - that is the ECB, tankan and payrolls," said Mark McFarland, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at UBS.  \par \par \uc2 "Expectations for an ECB rate cut are still there but for the ECB, until they get a clear picture on the economy, they don't want to start changing a rate profile aggressively."  \par \par \uc2 By 0745 GMT the euro was up a third of a percent against the dollar at $1.2200 having tumbled to this year's low of $1.2047 on Monday.  \par \par \uc2 Against the yen it was at 129.10 after hitting a four-month low of 127.21 in the previous session.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar was higher at 105.76 yen, having slipped to a six-week low of 105.23 on Monday.  \par \par \uc2 JAPAN'S \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  STANCE  \par \par \uc2 The yen zoomed higher on Monday after a British newspaper cited Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials as saying \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has officially ended.  \par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki repeated on Tuesday that Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy had not changed and that it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if market rates strayed from fundamentals.  \par \par \uc2 "Given that the dollar stopped its fall yesterday just above 105 (yen) on what looked like \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the market has decided that at least until the end of March it's a little risky to buy yen," said Mitsuo Imaizumi, deputy general manager of the international bond and \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  department at Daiwa Securities SMBC.  \par \par \uc2 Later on Tuesday, the U.S. consumer confidence index is due at 1500 GMT. Analysts say confidence has been undermined by a sluggish labour market, rising gasoline prices and security concerns after the Madrid bombings.  \par \par \uc2 Economists polled by Reuters on average expect the index to fall to 86.5 in March from 87.3 in February.  \par \par \uc2 U.S. non-farm payrolls on Friday are expected to have risen by around 100,000 in March, compared to a disappointing figure of 21,000 in the previous month.  \par \par \uc2 The previous employment report at the beginning of this month showed an increase in payrolls far smaller than expected, and reaffirmed the view the Fed will not have to raise official interest rates from 1.0 percent soon.  \par \par \uc2 Euro zone interest rates are currently 2.0 percent.   \par \par \uc2