\par\par \b \uc2 PREVIEW: BOJ Tankan To Show Econ Recovery Broadening  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Asako Tanabe  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 1,152 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 04:48\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The Bank of Japan's closely watched March tankan survey due Thursday will show Japan's economic recovery is gathering pace and broadening to previously weak non-manufacturing sectors, analysts say.  \par \par \uc2 Given surging exports and production plus a recent pickup in personal consumption, economists surveyed by Dow Jones and Nikkei News expect on average that the tankan's headline index of sentiment among big manufacturers will improve to 10, up from seven in the revised December survey.  \par \par \uc2 Perhaps more significantly, economists on average expect the BOJ's index measuring sentiment among large non-manufacturers will turn positive for the first time since November 1996, rising four points to a reading of four.  \par \par \uc2 Large manufacturers themselves predicted in December that their sentiment index would edge slightly lower to six in March while non-manufacturers expected a rise to four.  \par \par \uc2 The BOJ calculates the diffusion indexes by subtracting the percentage of respondents saying business conditions are bad from those saying they are good.  \par \par \uc2 All of the economists surveyed forecast that the diffusion indexes for both large manufacturers and non-manufacturers will post positive readings for the first time since November 1996.  \par \par \uc2 "The financial markets are already starting to factor in (positive tankan results) and expectations will rise for a further recovery of the economy," said Shuji Shirota, economist at Dresdner Kleinwort Wasserstein.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par      BOJ Revises Survey Methodology \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As