\par\par \b \uc2 Japan Tanigaki: No Change To Japan's  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Stance  \b0\par\par\uc2 273 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 02:57\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Japan's finance minister Tuesday repeated that there has been no shift in Tokyo's stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, brushing aside growing speculation the government is ending its massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaign to weaken the yen.  \par \par \uc2 "There is no change to our basic stance that \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates should move stably in reflection of fundamentals," Sadakazu Tanigaki told a regular news conference. "If movements don't reflect fundamentals, we will take appropriate action."  \par \par \uc2 Tanigaki added that media reports that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has decided to end large-scale \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  were based on speculation. [ 30-03-04 0110GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 An article Monday in the Times of London cited unnamed Bank of Japan officials as saying Japan's recovery is strong enough to withstand further yen gains, that Tokyo has decided there is no need to weaken the yen artificially and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  only when there's extraordinary volatility.  \par \par \uc2 "I think it is appropriate to say this article is based on speculation," Tanigaki said Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 As for how he viewed current economic fundamentals in Japan, Tanigaki said he believed there was "some light at the end of the tunnel" regarding the nation's efforts to overcome deflation.  \par \par \uc2 But he was quick to add the government will not let its guard down on the economy, suggesting that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  is prepared to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if it believes the yen has strengthened in a way that may harm Japan's recovery.  \par \par \uc2 -By Miyako Takebe, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; miyako.takebe@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Kirsty Mackenzie and John Gibson [ 30-03-04 0145GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040330e03u0000v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
