\par\par \b \uc2 Euro hits '04 low vs dollar in Europe, down on yen.  \b0\par\par\uc2 360 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 09:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, March 29 (Reuters) - The euro fell in Monday's early European trade to its lowest level this year against the dollar and set a four-month low against the yen on jitters the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could cut interest rates this week.  \par \par \uc2 The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also got a boost from a newspaper report - denied by the Bank of Japan and the finance ministry - that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had ended its massive yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaign because the economy no longer needed propping up.  \par \par \uc2 The report, published on the Web site of the Times of London, made dollar bulls nervous about Japan's future dollar purchases and yen selling after the country sold more than 30 trillion yen in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets since early 2003.  \par \par \uc2 At 0710 GMT the euro shed almost 0.50 percent on the day against the dollar, hitting its lowest level this year at $1.2050 . Versus the yen, the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lost one percent on the day to 127.26 , its lowest level since the middle of November.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar was down 0.30 percent against the yen to 105.58 after hitting a six-week low near 105.20 earlier.  \par \par \uc2 Debt markets are pricing in a small chance of an ECB rate cut from the current level of 2.0 percent, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meets on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 Little economic data is set for release on Monday, but Bank of Greece Governor Nicholas Garganas is scheduled to hold a news conference on the bank's economic policy report at 1030 GMT and Federal Reserve Bank of San Francisco President Robert Parry speaks at 1740 GMT.  \par \par \uc2 Earlier on Monday, data from the GfK market research group showed German consumer sentiment stagnating in April, underscoring concerns about euro zone's economic recovery.  \par \par \uc2 Worries over the sustainability of the recovery were fanned last week Germany's closely-watched Ifo institute showed business climate slightly below expectations and urged the ECB to cut rates.  \par \par \uc2 The forward looking GfK indicator, based on a survey of 2,00 Germans, was unchanged in April from a downwardly revised 5.1 in March.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040329e03t000so\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
