\par\par \b \uc2 CORRECTED - CORRECTED-Yen rises on newspaper report  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  over.  \b0\par\par\uc2 552 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 04:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     In TOKYO story headlined "Yen rises on newspaper report\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  over" please read in 7th paragraph ....surged\par  against the euro to a 4-=   month high.... instead of ....surged\par  against the euro to a 4-=   year high... (correcting period of\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 time).  \f28 \par \par \uc2 A corrected story follows.  \par \par \uc2 By Mariko Hayashibara  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, March 29 (Reuters) - The yen rose to a five-week high against the dollar on Monday, boosted after a British newspaper reported that Japan had ended its campaign to weaken its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The yen jumped to 105.26 per dollar, but quickly retreated to the day's low around 105.77 on what market sources said was dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "Many still think the authorities will protect the 105 yen level for the year-end on March 31," said Yoshihiro Nomura, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  section manager at Trust & Custody Services Bank in Tokyo.  \par \par \uc2 A senior official at the Finance Ministry declined to comment on whether it ordered the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Monday, but he said Tokyo would continue its policy of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  if needed.  \par \par \uc2 "We have been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  all along based on the Boca Raton statement (by Group of Seven countries) - that excessive volatility and disorderly movement are undesirable - and we will continue to do so if necessary," he told Reuters.  \par \par \uc2 At 0103 GMT, the dollar was 105.59/64 yen compared with 105.98 yen late in New York on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 The Japanese unit also surged against the euro to a 4-= month high of around 127.50 yen before trimming gains to trade at 127.90/95.  \par \par \uc2 MINISTRY IN CONTROL  \par \par \uc2 Many traders were roiled by a report on the Web site of the Times newspaper shortly after they returned to office early on Monday.  \par \par \uc2 Quoting Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials, the report said Tokyo's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaign, which has provoked criticism in Washington and deep concern in London, was thought by Japanese officials to be no longer necessary because the country's economic recovery is gathering strength.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has repeatedly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken a yen that has strengthened while the dollar has suffered a two-year downtrend.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said the market took the story as a cue to sell the dollar as it cited comments made in an "exclusive briefing", suggesting the report was more concrete than recent reports speculating that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  was slowing down its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 But the Finance Ministry official shrugged off the Times report, noting that it was the ministry that controlled Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, not the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the market eased off pushing up the yen because any media report quoting BOJ sources would not cause long-term panic because the Finance Ministry decides \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy.  \par \par \uc2 "So, just because the London Times has reported this, I think it is unlikely that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will step back from its extensive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy," said Robert Rennie, chief strategist with Westpac Bank, Sydney.  \par \par \uc2 While many dealers assume Japan will keep protecting the 105 yen level, they also ponder how far Japan would tolerate the yen edging up on economic recovery.  \par \par \uc2 The 105 yen level is the rate forecasted by many of Japan's major exporters such as auto firms for the second half of the current business year.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040329e03t0008n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
