\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3-Japan denies  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  policy shift, market tests resolve.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Mariko Hayashibara  \par \uc2 689 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 08:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, March 29 (Reuters) - Japanese officials sought to quell talk of a change in their policy of curbing the yen on Monday as the market tested their resolve, seizing on a newspaper report that Tokyo has ended its colossal market forays.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's large-scale \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the start of last year to hold down the strength of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has drawn criticism from its global trade partners and is also seen as unsustainable over the long run, leading to persistent speculation that it will at some point at least have to scale it back.  \par \par \uc2 Such speculation flared up on Monday after a report in the Times of London, quoting a Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  official, said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaign had "officially" ended. That sent the yen to five-week highs within reach of last month's 3-= highs.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) officials, saying \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy is under the jurisdiction of the ministry and not the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , flatly denied the report and vowed to continue \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market as needed.  \par \par \uc2 "It is a speculative article. There is no change in our policy," Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki told Reuters as he arrived in parliament for an Upper House committee meeting.  \par \par \uc2 His staff said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was in line with a Group of Seven (G7) statement issued at a meeting in Boca Raton, Florida, last month that said excessive volatility was undesirable.  \par \par \uc2 "We have been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  all along based on the Boca Raton statement - that excessive volatility and disorderly movements are undesirable - and we will continue to do so if necessary," a senior MOF official said.  \par \par \uc2 Japan has sold more than 30 trillion yen ($285 billion) in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the start of last year in a bid to rein in the buoyant yen. But the yen still rose to 3-1/2-year highs near 105.10 to the dollar last month, up more than 10 percent from lows near 120 set last August.  \par \par \uc2 Japanese officials worry that a strong yen could hurt exports and undermine an economic recovery.  \par \par \uc2 IN MARKET AGAIN?  \par \par \uc2 After opening sharply lower on the Times report, the dollar rose, with dealers citing renewed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the force behind the initial rebound. The MOF official declined to confirm if it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday.  \par \par \uc2 The Times quoted the BOJ official as saying Japan was "confident the Japanese recovery no longer depends on export strength...the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  have served their purpose".  \par \par \uc2 The MOF official said: "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy is set by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 . I don't know what the BOJ is saying (in the Times report) but people should ask us (about \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy)."  \par \par \uc2 A BOJ spokesman echoed that view, saying the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not in a position to comment on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy. He said the BOJ could not confirm what was said in the Times story.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds come from the MOF's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  special account. When \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  takes place, the ministry places orders with the BOJ, which then makes the transactions in the market as an agent bank.  \par \par \uc2 The MOF official also played down speculation that the ministry may no longer feel a need to keep the yen down once book-closings for most Japanese corporations are over at the end of Japan's financial year on March 31.  \par \par \uc2 "There seems to be a lot of talk about a policy change in March or April, but there is no change in our \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Robert Rennie, chief strategist with Westpac Bank in Sydney, said the reported comments reflected growing unease within the BOJ about the effects on monetary policy of the huge \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "Just because the London Times has reported this, I think it is unlikely that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will step back from its extensive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy," he said.  \par \par \uc2 "But this is another piece of evidence to suggest that the love affair that has existed between (BOJ Governor Toshihiko) Fukui since he took over and the MOF is beginning to show signs of fraying." ($1=105.28 yen) (Additional reporting by Ritsuko Ando).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040329e03t0005r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
