\par\par \b \uc2 Japan Tanigaki: No Change To Japan  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Policy  \b0\par\par\uc2 248 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 05:52\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy remains unchanged, Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki said Monday, dismissing as speculation a newspaper report that Tokyo has ended its campaign to counter the yen's strength.  \par \par \uc2 Tanigaki denied a Times of London report citing unnamed Bank of Japan sources as saying Tokyo has decided that there is no more need to weaken the yen through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "It's an article based on speculation," Tanigaki told Dow Jones Newswires. Asked if Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy had changed, he said, "No, it hasn't."  \par \par \uc2 The Times report also cited the BOJ officials as indicating they will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market only when there's extraordinary volatility. The sources "made clear that the unprecedented dollar purchases of the past seven months were formally over", the newspaper reported.  \par \par \uc2 But the BOJ acts only as the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 's agent in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  and has no authority over \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy under the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  Law.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar fell to a low of Y105.29 - within striking distance of a three-year low of Y105.16 - as traders reacted to the report.  \par \par \uc2 But it later recovered amid speculation it was unlikely the MOF would withdraw completely from the market, especially at current levels. At 0400 GMT, it as trading at Y105.56.  \par \par \uc2 -By Jonathan Soble, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; jonathan.soble@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Bennett Richardson [ 29-03-04 0405GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040329e03t0005l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
