\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  ends yen-dlr  \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention \highlight\uc2 -paper.   \b0\par\par\uc2 304 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 00:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  LONDON, March 28 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 150-billion-pound ($273 billion) campaign to weaken the yen and strengthen the dollar has officially come to an end, the Times newspaper reported, citing sources at the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 .    \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaign, which has provoked criticism in Washington and deep concern in London, is thought by Japanese officials to be no longer necessary because the country's economic recovery is gathering strength, the London Times newspaper reported in its March 29 edition.    \par \par \uc2  BOJ sources said that they would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the markets only when there was extraordinary volatility, but made clear that the unprecedented dollar purchases of the past seven months were formally over, the paper reported.    \par \par \uc2  The BOJ and Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  will no longer buy dollars even to smooth out the sort of sudden price spikes that have prompted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past, it added.    \par \par \uc2  "Even if the market shows volatility, we believe that things are not so fragile now," the BOJ sources said, in what the paper describes as an exclusive briefing.    \par \par \uc2  "We have reached the point where we are confident that the Japanese recovery no longer depends on export strength ... the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  have served their purpose," the sources added.    \par \par \uc2  The dollar was last quoted at 105.35  at 2230 GMT.    \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  drive to support the falling dollar against the yen began in earnest last September, and has left Japan with paper trading losses of more than 50 billion pounds, the paper said.    \par \par \uc2  The end of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has apparently been brought about by Toshihiko Fukui, the BOJ governor, who has restored confidence in the Japanese economy since his appointment a year ago and won plaudits from international financial authorities for his deft monetary management, the paper said. ($1=.5502 Pound).    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040328e03s00c77\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
