\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  MOF Official: No Change To  \highlight22\uc2 FX Intervention \highlight\uc2  Stance  \b0\par\par\uc2 437 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 01:20\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is set solely by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , remains unchanged, a MOF official said Monday, downplaying a newspaper report that Tokyo's campaign to support the dollar has come to an end.  \par \par \uc2 "We haven't changed our policy on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," an official at the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets division told Dow Jones Newswires when asked about a report in the Times of London, which cited Bank of Japan officials as saying the government believes the country's economic and export outlook is positive and there is no more need to weaken the yen artificially.  \par \par \uc2 "It's true that both the BOJ and the MOF think the economy is recovering," the MOF official said. "But as far as \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is concerned, the BOJ has absolutely no authority at all."  \par \par \uc2 Japan MOF officials maintain that \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates should move stably in reflection of economic fundamentals, but that the ministry will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets if movements stray from such fundamentals. [ 28-03-04 2350GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Recent media articles have indicated BOJ officials are seeking an exit to the massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaign from last January, during which the government spent more than Y30 trillion to keep the yen from strengthening.  \par \par \uc2 The Times article quotes unnamed Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  sources as indicating they will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market only when there's extraordinary volatility. The sources "made clear that the unprecedented dollar purchases of the past seven months were formally over", the newspaper reports.  \par \par \uc2 But the MOF official made it clear Monday that "the MOF is the sole authority in charge of setting \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy."  \par \par \uc2 In \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , only the Minister of Finance is legally authorized to conduct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to achieve \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate stability as stipulated by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Foreign Trade Law. The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  executes \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in accordance with the directions of the Minister under the Bank of Japan Law as the MOF's agent.  \par \par \uc2 In public, BOJ Governor Toshihiko Fukui has publicly backed up the MOF's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , saying that the government's efforts to weaken the yen aren't inconsistent with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's easing policies.  \par \par \uc2 But the recent reports citing BOJ officials suggest there might be a rift between the MOF and the BOJ regarding \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , possibly because \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may make it more difficult for the BOJ to eventually exit its ultra-easy monetary policy.  \par \par \uc2 -By Miyako Takebe, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; miyako.takebe@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Kirsty Mackenzie and Bennett Richardson [ 29-03-04 0039GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040328e03s0005c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
