\par\par \b \uc2 Tracking euro no longer surefire bet for gold traders.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Gertrude Chavez  \par \uc2 697 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 18:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, March 26 (Reuters) - The high correlation that has existed between gold and the euro for the last two years, has come under increasing pressure, as volatility in the U.S. dollar, makes the gold trade more difficult.  \par \par \uc2 Until a few weeks ago, a rise in the euro against the dollar had been mirrored by an increase in the price of gold, as demand for the yellow metal rose among more risk-averse global investors.  \par \par \uc2 Gold, which is priced in dollars, becomes more affordable in terms of other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  falls. The euro, being a highly liquid \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , became the benchmark for gold as the value of the euro became a more generally accepted measure of the dollar's weakness.  \par \par \uc2 More recently, however, gold's correlation with the euro has ruptured as the yellow metal gained a momentum of its own, rising steadily despite a fall in the single European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid escalating geopolitical tensions.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts say that gold has instead developed a nascent, albeit inconclusive, correlation with Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , specifically the yen.  \par \par \uc2 "There has been a change in emphasis. Gold, which rises when the greenback falls, has been looking to other appreciating \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to express weakness in the dollar," said Kamal Naqvi, precious metals analyst at Barclays Capital.  \par \par \uc2 "The obvious place to look for that broadening weakness is in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , led by the yen," he added.  \par \par \uc2 As gold prices surged in the last few weeks, the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  retreated, hurt by a chorus of remarks from European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials expressing dismay over the euro's export-damaging advance against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Comments from several officials of the ECB raised the prospect of a cut in interest rates, a prospect that would be bearish for the single European unit since it lowers the yields on euro-denominated assets, diminishing their appeal to investors.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The euro, as a result, has fallen from its record high above $1.2900\par against the dollar posted in February to $1.2155 on Friday. By\par contrast, spot gold eased back to $420.40 after it has climbed to\par $422.80        per ounce on Friday, the highest in more than a month.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A BEELINE FOR GOLD, YEN LINK  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Gold has outperformed the euro in the past two weeks and is now about 1.5 percent away from its important resistance zone," said Jes Black, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  analyst at MG Financial.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investors flocked to the gold market amid heightened security worries that resurfaced amid the fatal bombings in Madrid in early March and several bomb scares in the United States and Europe in the last few weeks.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Analysts say that these incidents are yet another reminder that the U.S. war against terrorism is far from over and could propel gold higher in the near to medium term.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Apart from flight-to-safety buying, firmer gold prices reflect the commodity's strong underlying fundamentals. "This suggests that North Asian demand for gold and other metals is still rampant and that the supply side remains very tight," said Richard Franulovich, senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at Westpac Banking Corp.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Analysts say that in the face of the euro's sluggish performance, the gold market has started to monitor the yen's robust price action.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The revival of economic growth in Japan has attracted hefty foreign equity investments that would have pushed the yen to far loftier levels if not for the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's yen-weakening \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  - a strategy aimed at gaining export advantage.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Last week alone, foreigners bought a massive $11 billion in Japanese stocks, the largest weekly volume since March 1999, according to IDEAglobal.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese news reports earlier this month suggesting that the BoJ might scale back its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fueled some beefy yen gains, in tandem with gold. The dollar has slipped against the yen, falling to 105.56 yen on Friday from around 112 yen earlier this month.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Barclays' Naqvi, however, was quick to point out that the yen's emerging link with gold was far from solid, but he conceded that the budding trend "does reflect increased market expectations that Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will appreciate."   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040326e03q002gc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
