\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro up from lows vs dlr, yen - still vulnerable.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Burton Frierson  \par \uc2 727 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 14:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, March 25 (Reuters) - The euro bounced off four-month lows against the yen and three-week lows versus the dollar on Thursday but looked vulnerable ahead on rate cut speculation while growing economic confidence supported the yen.  \par \par \uc2 Hints on Tuesday and Wednesday by European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials that an interest rate cut would not be out of the question if consumer spending failed to pick up remained fresh in investors' minds.  \par \par \uc2 The yen, already buoyed by upbeat growth figures and an upgrade to Japan's outlook from Standard & Poor's, got further support from Thursday's data showing record foreign buying of Japanese stocks, helping it to one-month highs beyond 106.00 per dollar.  \par \par \uc2 "The story is that the yen is being driven higher by optimism on the Japanese economy and overseas investors buying the recovery," said Adam Cole, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Credit Agricole Indosuez.  \par \par \uc2 "It does look very much like the ECB is laying the foundations for getting rates down. That is what hit the euro. Given we still have some way to go in terms of fully discounting a rate cut then there is probably more of that to come."  \par \par \uc2 By 1245 GMT, the euro traded a flat on the day at $1.2125, after earlier weakening to $1.2100. It lost two cents on Wednesday after the dovish ECB comments.  \par \par \uc2 Against the yen it traded flat at 128.75 yen while the dollar also managed to hold steady on the day at 106.20 yen after earlier falling to 105.78 yen, its weakest since February 18.  \par \par \uc2 U.S. initial jobless claims are due at 1330 GMT, with analysts predicting 335,000 new filings. Revised fourth quarter U.S. gross domestic product figures are also due at 1330 GMT.  \par \par \uc2 POLICYMAKERS ON THE PLATFORM  \par \par \uc2 Markets will watch ECB President Jean-Claude Trichet's speech in the U.S. at 2100 GMT to see if he expands on comments to a German business newspaper on Tuesday about the ECB's worries on consumer spending.  \par \par \uc2 These were the comments that prompted the euro's initial losses on Wednesday after other ECB voices chimed in.  \par \par \uc2 "There has been quite an important shift in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market sentiment on interest rate views," said Tony Norfield, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  research at ABN AMRO.  \par \par \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan speaks at 1400 GMT, Treasury Secretary John Snow at 1500 GMT and a batch of Fed officials, including New York Fed President Timothy Geithner and St. Louis President William Poole all take the podium later in the day.  \par \par \uc2 YEN POPULARITY  \par \par \uc2 Traders are trying to fathom why Japanese authorities have not stepped in heavily to block yen gains against the dollar this week after they spent record amounts of yen last year and in the first two months of this year to stop it from rising.  \par \par \uc2 "Fundamentals are very, very bullish for the Japanese yen, there's no doubt about it," said Hans Redeker, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at BNP Paribas.  \par \par \uc2 "In April, when we get the numbers concerning the amount of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  for March, I believe it will show it was just a fraction of what we saw in February," said BNP's Redeker.  \par \par \uc2 Some market sources said the authorities, acting through the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  intermittently in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Thursday, selling the yen and buying dollars.  \par \par \uc2 Japan's top financial diplomat Zembei Mizoguchi said Tokyo's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy was unchanged, reminding the market yet again that it was ready to act.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers noted global funds keep flowing into Japan, with foreigners buying a record 1.1483 trillion yen ($11 billion) of Japanese stocks in the week ended March 19.  \par \par \uc2 The yen was also seen getting a minor boost from better-than-expected Japanese trade balance data for February, with the surplus rising 51.7 percent from a year earlier.  \par \par \uc2 Elsewhere sterling fell more than one percent from late New York levels against the dollar and euro after Bank of England Governor Mervyn King pointed to the risk of the pound's appreciation to UK growth.  \par \par \uc2 Sterling has been buoyed in recent months by speculation that interest rates have further to rise after two hikes in November and February which took UK rates to 4.0 percent.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040325e03p002h2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
