\par\par \b \uc2 Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dollar Falls Vs Yen On Yen's Strength Vs Euro  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Leika Kihara  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 617 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 06:45\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The dollar fell to a five-week low against the yen in Asia Thursday, weighed down by cross-trading pressure from the yen's strength against the euro as traders grew more upbeat about Japan's economic prospects.  \par \par \uc2 After an early climb to near Y106.50 on bids apparently placed by a U.S. investment bank, the dollar turned down and fell as low as Y105.91, breaking below the psychologically key Y106 mark for the first time since mid-February.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar soon bounced back to just above that level, but traders said there was no sign Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  was placing covert bids to support the U.S. unit.  \par \par \uc2 Many traders said the dollar's tumble against the yen was driven by the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise against the euro, as European players continue to shift funds into Japan's well-performing stock market.  \par \par \uc2 Mounting speculation - fueled by recent comments from senior European officials - that the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may cut interest rates soon, also weighed on the euro, briefly sending it below Y128.30 before it recovered some ground to around Y128.60.  \par \par \uc2 At 0515 GMT, the dollar was quoted at Y106.06, below Y106.25 late Wednesday in New York. The dollar was at Y106.67 late Wednesday in Tokyo.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was at $1.2130, higher than $1.2125 late Wednesday in New York. The euro was at $1.2314 in Tokyo Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y128.62, down from Y128.80 in New York late Wednesday. The euro was at Y131.39 in Tokyo late Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 Sterling was at $1.8246, up from $1.8238 in New York but lower than $1.8475 in Tokyo Wednesday. [ 25-03-04 0545GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 The dollar resumed its slide below Y106 later Thursday, briefly touching a low of Y105.75. This left some traders doubtful as to whether the MOF was still serious about defending any "line in the sand," be it Y106 or Y105.  \par \par \uc2 "I still think the MOF will step in if the dollar falls near Y105.00," a trader at a Japanese brokerage house said. "But it's no longer a sure thing" because of growing signs of brightness in Japan's economy, which makes it tougher for the MOF to justify yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he said.  \par \par \uc2 Upbeat views about \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economy grew after Standard & Poor's Wednesday raised its outlook on Japan to stable from negative, citing an improving outlook for economic growth.  \par \par \uc2 Data released Thursday showed Japan's merchandise trade surplus in February jumped 51.7% from a year earlier to Y1.407 trillion, underscoring robust export growth is keeping the economy on a recovery path.  \par \par \uc2 Masamichi Koike, head of spot \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at Sumitomo Mitsui Banking, expects yen-buying pressure to remain strong, leaving room for the dollar to test Y105 as early as next week.  \par \par \uc2 "With so many positive factors out for the Japanese economy, I don't see an end to the inflow of overseas funds into Japanese markets any time soon," Koike said.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    -By Leika Kihara, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; leika.kihara@dowjones.com   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Kirsty Mackenzie  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The chart of late Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates that accompanied Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been replaced with an enhanced \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fixture that is updated hourly.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Subscribers can find this table:  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX [ 25-03-04 0705GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1074  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040325e03p00060\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
