\par\par \b \uc2 Dollar drifts as security concerns weighed.   \b0\par\par\uc2 499 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 02:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  TOKYO, March 24 (Reuters) - The dollar drifted sideways against major rivals on Wednesday, as the market searched for direction and awaited the next phase of the heated-up conflict in the Middle East.    \par \par \uc2  Israel vowed to kill more top Palestinian militants on Tuesday, just days after its assassination of Ahmed Yassin, leader of the Palestinian group Hamas, prompted threats of revenge against Israel and the United States.    \par \par \uc2  "The market is a little nervous with all the geopolitical tensions out there, and as a result the dlr/yen and other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are struggling for direction now," said Junya Tanase, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at JP Morgan Chase.    \par \par \uc2  Traders said that rising security concerns were a negative factor for the dollar, but that market wariness about \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  was discouraging yen bulls, trapping the dollar/yen rate in a tight range.    \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading at 106.78/86 yen as of 0104 GMT, slightly up from 106.73 in late New York trade on Tuesday.    \par \par \uc2  Tanase said barring any unexpected shocks to the dollar, it would likely stay in a range around 106-107.5 yen ahead of the release next Thursday of Japan's closely watched "tankan" survey of business sentiment.    \par \par \uc2  The euro was slightly up at $1.2365 compared with 1.2330.    \par \par \uc2  It fell as low as $1.2269 in New York trade after European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Jean-Claude Trichet said in an interview with German newspaper Handelsblatt that consumer confidence in the euro zone was weaker than it should be at this stage of an upswing.    \par \par \uc2  The ECB would reassess its outlook for a gradual recovery if consumer spending fails to pick up, he said.    \par \par \uc2  Sterling climbed to a two-week high of $1.8539 supported by strong economic data and hawkish statements by Bank of England officials, which have increased market speculation that the BoE may lift interest rates at its April policy meeting.    \par \par \uc2  Most analysts still see the dollar resuming its downtrend this year, after recent comments from U.S. Federal Reserve officials, who signalled the Fed would be patient in raising U.S. interest rates from current four-decade lows.    \par \par \uc2  Speculation is also building that a recent flow of upbeat news on Japan's economy will make it increasingly hard for Tokyo to justify a continuation of its aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy - especially ahead of a Washington G7 meeting in late April.    \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent some 30 trillion yen ($281 billion) on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the 14 months to the end of February to help prevent a strengthening yen from derailing its export-led economic recovery.    \par \par \uc2  The market was awaiting reports on U.S. durable goods orders and new home sales due later on Wednesday.    \par \par \uc2  Analysts polled by Reuters forecast a median rise of 1.7 percent in orders for expensive factory goods in February after a sharp fall in demand for cars and aircraft in January dragged overall orders down 2.3 percent. ($1=106.69 yen).    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040324e03o00070\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
