   \par \par \uc2  further. (ECONOMY-KOREA-GDP (UPDATE 2) moved at 0420, by Rhee     \par \par \uc2  So-eui, 592 words)     \par \par \uc2  MELBOURNE - BHP Billiton Ltd/Plc approves the $1.4 billion     \par \par \uc2  development of the Ravensthorpe nickel mine and expansion of     \par \par \uc2  the Yabulu refinery in Australia to meet strong world nickel     \par \par \uc2  demand. (MINERALS-BHPBILLITON-NICKEL (UPDATE 3), expect by     \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     SEE ALSO: (MINERALS-AUSTRALIA-BHP-NICKEL (UPDATE 1), moved\par at 0247, by James Regan 600 words)\par     TOKYO - U.S. chip maker Lattice Semiconductor Corp plans to\par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par invest between $100 million and $200 million in a new Fujitsu\par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par semiconductor factory, a vote of confidence in the Japanese\par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par electronics conglomerate's chip-making technology.\par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (TECH-FUJITSU-LATTICE (UPDATE 3), expect by 0530, by Kiyoshi\par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Takenaka, 600 words)\par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SINGAPORE - Asian share markets recover some poise as\par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par selling eases in Taiwan and the dollar steadies after global\par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par security fears hit Wall Street. (MARKETS-GLOBAL (WRAPUP 3),\par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - - - -\par     COMPANIES\par     SINGAPORE - China's largest state oil and gas firm,\par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PetroChina, is building a 360,000 tonne-per-year ethylene plant\par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par costing $575 million in the remote, underdeveloped northwest\par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par that is due for completion by 2006, China-based industry\par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sources say (ENERGY-CHINA-PETROCHINA (UPDATE 1), expect by\par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0600, by Chen Aizhu, 400 words)\par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TOKYO - Japan's move to set up an agency to speed up drug\par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par approvals is a boon for pharmaceutical companies companies\par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par eager to sell new medicine in the world's second-biggest drug\par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market. (HEALTH-JAPAN-DRUGAPPROVAL, expect by 0700, by Yuka\par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Obayashi, 800 words)\par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par KAMEYAMA, Japan - Kameyama in western Japan once found\par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par prosperity as a place where samurai warriors rested on the walk\par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from Tokyo to the old capital of Kyoto; 400 years later, the\par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par good times are back thanks to Sharp Corp's flagship plant for\par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par making flat-screen TVs, which has drawn more high-tech firms to\par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the area. (TECH-JAPAN-RENEWAL (BUSINESS FEATURE), moved at\par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - - - -\par     MARKETS/ECONOMY\par     HONG KONG - The IMF says China's huge accumulation of\par     \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves cannot be sustained without\par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par inflationary pressures and that limited exchange rate\par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par flexibility would not pose significant risks to its economy.\par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (ECONOMY-CHINA-IMF, expect by 0700, by Paul Caine, 600 words)\par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par - ~- --.\par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040323e03n000pa\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
