\par\par \b \uc2 Treasuries benefit as global tension sinks stocks.  \b0\par\par\uc2 583 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 15:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, March 22 (Reuters) - Treasuries prices rose on Monday, breaking three sessions of losses, as geopolitical concerns seemed to shake stocks and benefit safe-haven U.S. government debt.  \par \par \uc2 European equities sank near to their lowest levels for the year while sharp falls in stock futures pointed to a troubled start for Wall Street.  \par \par \uc2 The pressure was linked in part to Israel's killing of the spiritual leader of the Hamas Islamic militant group, Sheikh Ahmed Yassin, in its highest profile assassination of more than three years of conflict.  \par \par \uc2 The killing stirred feSwiss franc.  \par \par \uc2 That was just as well for bond bulls since technical tides were trying to erode some of the market's recent hefty gains.  \par \par \uc2 "With the market having failed to penetrate 3.65 percent, there is room for a backup into the 3.80's, perhaps as far as 3.90," said Richard Gilhooly, fixed-income strategist at BNP Paribas, referring to the 10-year note yield, while adding there had been plenty of buying on dips so far.  \par \par \uc2 Early Monday, the benchmark 10-year note was yielding 3.76 percent, compared to 3.77 percent late on Friday and 4.10 percent this time last month.  \par \par \uc2 There were no U.S. economic data due Monday to offer a distraction, but two top Federal Reserve officials are appearing. Traders hope one or other may expand on last week's policy statement in which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  surprised many by taking a slightly less bullish stance on the economy and jobs.  \par \par \uc2 The Fed's caution encouraged the market to further reduce the risk of a tightening this year and sparked a sizable rally in Treasuries.  \par \par \uc2 Both San Francisco President Robert Parry and Chicago Fed President Michael Moskow appear at 1.00 p.m. (1800 GMT) though only the latter is giving a formal speech on the economy.  \par \par \uc2 The last time Moskow spoke in February he said the Fed could afford to be patient on policy but warned that interest rates would have to rise at some point.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Five-year notes  were up 3/32 in price, taking yields to 2.71 percent\par from 2.74 percent on Friday. The 30-year bond             rose 9/32,\par leaving its yield at 4.69 percent from 4.71 percent.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The two-year note added 1/32, easing its yield down to 1.50 percent from 1.52 percent.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Treasury will hold an auction of new two-year notes on Wednesday, which traders expect will amount to $26 billion. The sale will be seen as a test of foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  demand now that the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  seems to be \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  less in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yen has risen sharply in the last week or so on speculation the Japanese authorities had decided to cut back on the massive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  conducted early in the year. That in turn has led to worries the BOJ will have less dollars with which to buy U.S. debt.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The auction will be a good opportunity to see if the BOJ is still going to back up the truck and load it with securities," said BNP's Gilhooly.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We suspect that even if the eventual plan is to slow down or stop \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , they have done enough recently that they will need to come for some two-year notes," he added.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 So far this year, offshore central banks have bought a whopping $100 billion in Treasury and agency debt.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040322e03m001rx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
