\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar rallies on hopes security fears will ease.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Gertrude Chavez  \par \uc2 593 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 19:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, March 19 (Reuters) - The dollar advanced in a jumpy market on Friday on hopes security tensions would ease after news Pakistani troops had closed in on a group of Islamic militants, possibly including a senior al Qaeda figure.  \par \par \uc2 Pakistan said its troops had surrounded between 300 and 400 rebels, both foreign militants and their Pakistani tribal allies, in a battle near the border with Afghanistan.  \par \par \uc2 Capturing al Qaeda number two man Ayman al-Zawahri, who may be among them, could bolster the U.S. anti-terrorism campaign and thereby boost the dollar, analysts said. Some believe al-Zawahri may have knowledge of planned attacks and may be crucial in capturing al Qaeda leader Osama bin Laden.  \par \par \uc2 "We're seeing a bounce-back in the dollar, at least against the euro, on the back of some hopes that the activity in Afghanistan will produce an al-Qaeda biggie," said Jeremy Fand, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at WestLB in New York.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar also rebounded amid profit-taking on the euro and other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  which had gained when a security alert in Europe the day before prompted safe-haven buying, analysts said.  \par \par \uc2 By midday in New York, the euro fell 1 percent against the dollar to $1.2279. The euro had spiked briefly earlier after news that Washington DC police were searching schools following a bomb threat made over the Internet.  \par \par \uc2 The single European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also down against the yen at 131.14 yen. Against the Swiss franc, which gains a bid in times of heightened geopolitical worries, the greenback rose to 1.2685 francs. Sterling fell to $1.8291.  \par \par \uc2 "I think it's a consolidation of yesterday's losses. Specifically we had a big move up in the euro against the dollar yesterday," said Shaun Osborne, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Scotia Capital in Toronto, explaining part of the reason for the dollar's recovery on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 GAUGING JAPAN  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded above this week's one-month low against the yen, with traders unwilling to test Japan's tolerance of a higher yen any further.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar firmed against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in midday trade to 106.84 yen.  \par \par \uc2 The market was nervous about the limits of Japan's patience over a potentially export-damaging rise in the yen against the dollar, after a two-yen gain on the greenback on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said that since the data schedule for Friday is thin, the market would trade on technical levels, geopolitical events and any hints of Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 They said the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been conspicuous by its absence this week after months of yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Some traders said the dollar's downside against the yen was limited now unless the market could take out 106.50 yen. But some analysts do not rule out BoJ action in the near future.  \par \par \uc2 "The dollar found a temporary bottom against the yen at 106.30 with the risk/reward of being square to long (position) better as most anticipate the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively should we fall to 105 yen," said Andrew Busch, global \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at BMO Nesbitt Burns in Chicago.  \par \par \uc2 Long positions are effectively bets that a specific \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will rise.  \par \par \uc2 Traders were skeptical that a dollar blip higher in the Tokyo afternoon, which took it up to 107.30 yen, stemmed from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Japanese authorities. Some said it was possible \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been back in the market but at much reduced levels.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040319e03j002g8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
