\par\par \b \uc2 Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Yen Retreats, But MOF's Stance Seen Weakening  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Jonathan Soble  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 755 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 06:37\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The yen retreated against the dollar and the euro in Asia Friday, despite intensifying speculation that Japan's authorities are abandoning their efforts to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Dollar and euro buying by Japanese investors helped lift both \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the yen, and traders said there was no sign of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from Tokyo.  \par \par \uc2 "Chalk it up to position squaring ahead of the weekend," said Satoshi Tate, a vice president for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at UFJ Bank. After strong gains by the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent sessions, conditions were ripe for a small retracement, he said.  \par \par \uc2 But he added that rising doubts over the commitment of Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the dollar mean the U.S. unit likely hasn't finished falling for now.  \par \par \uc2 "Someone's going to test the MOF's stance, it's just a matter of when," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Ministry officials spent Friday fending off questions over a local report that they are considering cutting back on yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The Mainichi Shimbun report hit the dollar overnight after the daily published an advance copy on its Web site.  \par \par \uc2 Citing "international financial sources" - possibly senior Japanese government officials - the report said the government has judged that the days of using massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a means to support the economy are coming to an end.  \par \par \uc2 In response, Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki said Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy hasn't changed and Tokyo will continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if markets stray from economic fundamentals.  \par \par \uc2 His deputy, Vice Minister for International Affairs Zembei Mizoguchi, dismissed the report as "speculative talk." He said Japanese policy remains guided by the statement issued by Group of Seven finance chiefs in Boca Raton, Florida, in early February warning against "excess volatility and disorderly movements" in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates.  \par \par \uc2 "We'll take firm action in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets if necessary," Mizoguchi told reporters.  \par \par \uc2 Many analysts weren't convinced.  \par \par \uc2 "It's likely that the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities have retreated amid criticism by the U.S. of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy," said Tohru Sasaki, a strategist at J.P. Morgan in Tokyo.  \par \par \uc2 J.P. Morgan forecasts put the dollar at Y100 by the end of June, Y97 by the end of September and Y99 by the end of the year.  \par \par \uc2 At 0515 GMT, the dollar was quoted at Y107.09, above Y106.75 late Thursday in New York. The dollar was at Y106.94 late Thursday in Tokyo.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was at $1.2397, slightly higher than $1.2390 late Thursday in New York. The euro was at $1.2281 in Tokyo Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y132.80, up from Y132.20 in New York late Thursday. The euro was at Y131.32 in Tokyo late Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 Sterling was at $1.8342, up marginally from $1.8340 in New York but lower than $1.8262 in Tokyo Thursday. [ 19-03-04 0537GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 UFJ's Tate said the Mainichi report, which followed a similar story in a financial daily earlier this week, may be part of a deliberate effort by the ministry to gauge public reaction to a possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  pullback.  \par \par \uc2 He noted that U.S. officials including Treasury Secretary John Snow have recently expressed concern over Japan's massive yen sales, while Tanigaki has been grilled in parliament over the fiscal implications of borrowing to finance \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "The MOF's stance has been criticized by the U.S. and scrutinized by parliament," Tate said. "So how does the public at large feel?"  \par \par \uc2 The answer could shape ministry policy, he said.  \par \par \uc2 "If they detect a sense of crisis over yen appreciation, they could say 'Look, we've got allies in this."'  \par \par \uc2 On the other hand, if the public have grown less fearful of a "high-yen recession," ministry officials may feel they can allow the dollar to fall further without prompting a political backlash.  \par \par \uc2 "Psychology has always been an important part of the exchange rate issue," he said.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    -By Jonathan Soble, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; jonathan.soble@dowjones.com   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Alastair Gale  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The chart of late Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates that accompanied Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been replaced with an enhanced \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fixture that is updated hourly.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Subscribers can find this table:  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX [ 19-03-04 0606GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1074  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040319e03j0005y\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (japan near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Datum\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 01/01/1995 bis 21/08/2023\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\